cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AvantGraph, please cite it using the metadata below. The system is described in the VLDB 2022 demo paper; its query optimizer is described in the VLDB Journal 2025 paper."
title: "AvantGraph"
abstract: "AvantGraph is a high-performance property-graph processing engine developed at TU/e. It executes Cypher queries with native support for graph-shaped intermediate representations, factorised joins, multi-threaded loading, and zero-copy disk reads. AvantGraph integrates the GraphAlg algorithm language for in-database iterative analytics, and exposes a GraphQL-based Lake API. In SciLake it serves all five pilot Scientific Knowledge Graphs (Cancer, Neuroscience, Energy, Transport-CCAM, Transport-Maritime) backed by the full OpenAIRE Graph."
